<section style="padding:72px 24px 40px;"><div style="max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;"><div class="rich"><p>A proper inverter installation is more than hanging a box on the wall. The installer sizes the inverter against your real load, matches the battery bank to the inverter's voltage, fits breakers, surge protection and earthing, and puts the batteries somewhere with air. This page walks through each step so you can read a quote line by line before light goes again and the gen is the only thing running.</p><p>Harmattan Solar Co is advertising for independent installers. It does not install or sell equipment itself, so the work, the warranty and the invoice belong to the installer who quotes your job. We cover <a href="/solar-installation-lagos/">Lagos</a>, <a href="/solar-installation-abuja/">Abuja</a>, <a href="/solar-installation-port-harcourt/">Port Harcourt</a>, <a href="/solar-installation-ibadan/">Ibadan</a>, <a href="/solar-installation-benin-city/">Benin City</a> and <a href="/solar-installation-enugu/">Enugu</a>. Call +234 809 000 0000 with your appliance list, and see <a href="/solar-system-price-nigeria/">published solar prices</a> to know what a fair quote looks like.</p></div></div></section>
<section style="padding:0 24px 64px;"><div style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;">
    <span class="kicker">What We Handle</span>
    <h2 class="section-heading" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,32px);margin:0 0 28px;">What's Included in Every Visit</h2>
    <div class="feat-grid" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:20px;">
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6DFCF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(31,34,49,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 8px;">Inverter and battery only</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">No panels yet? An inverter and battery bank charged from the grid is a valid starting point, and the installer can leave room to add panels later.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6DFCF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(31,34,49,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 8px;">Panels added later</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">A hybrid inverter has a built-in solar charge controller (MPPT), so panels can join the same box once money allows. Check its maximum panel input first.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6DFCF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(31,34,49,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 8px;">Tubular to lithium upgrade</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">If your tubular batteries no longer last the night, the installer checks whether your inverter accepts lithium at its voltage and charge settings before you pay for the battery.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6DFCF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(31,34,49,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 8px;">More battery capacity</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Need to run more overnight? The installer works out the extra kWh from your rating plates and says in writing whether new batteries can share a bank with old ones.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6DFCF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(31,34,49,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 8px;">Breakers, surge protection, earthing</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">NEMSA guidelines as reported in April 2026 list isolators, breakers or fuses, surge protection and earthing. Each should appear as a line on your quote.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #E6DFCF;border-radius:10px;padding:26px;box-shadow:0 2px 8px rgba(31,34,49,0.05);">
        <h3 style="font-family:'Plus Jakarta Sans',sans-serif;font-size:18px;font-weight:800;color:#1B1D2A;margin:0 0 8px;">A quote you can compare</h3>
        <p style="font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.7;color:#555;margin:0;">Exact inverter model, battery voltage and kWh, cable size, warranty years and VAT treatment, all written down, so two or three quotes can be compared like for like.</p>
      </div>
</div>
